 Skim 10 (NULL) — three-valued logic is a common surprise.",[82,839,841],{"id":840},"if-youre-coming-from-a-programming-language","If you're coming from a programming language",[15,843,844,845,848,849,852,853,856],{},"Read 06–09 (subqueries, CTEs, set ops, windows) — these are the \"control flow\" of SQL. Don't skip 10 (NULL) — ",[66,846,847],{},"NULL = NULL"," is ",[66,850,851],{},"UNKNOWN",", not ",[66,854,855],{},"TRUE",". Read 26 (EXPLAIN) early — query plans matter more than syntax.",[82,858,860],{"id":859},"if-youre-a-senior-engineer","If you're a senior engineer",[15,862,863],{},"Skim 01–14. Read 09 (Windows), 15 (Isolation), 18 (JSON), 19 (Recursive), 26 (EXPLAIN) closely. Use 27 (Patterns) and 29 (Pitfalls) as references. Read 28 (Admin) for production readiness.",[19,865,867],{"id":866},"companion-resources","Companion Resources",[57,869,870,879,887,895,903,911],{},[27,871,872,878],{},[117,873,877],{"href":874,"rel":875},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.postgresql.org\u002Fdocs\u002F",[876],"nofollow","PostgreSQL Docs"," — the reference implementation used in most examples.",[27,880,881,886],{},[117,882,885],{"href":883,"rel":884},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.sqlite.org\u002Fdocs.html",[876],"SQLite Docs"," — embedded SQL, great for learning.",[27,888,889,894],{},[117,890,893],{"href":891,"rel":892},"https:\u002F\u002Fuse-the-index-luke.com",[876],"Use The Index, Luke"," — indexing explained deeply.",[27,896,897,902],{},[117,898,901],{"href":899,"rel":900},"https:\u002F\u002Fsql-performance-explained.com",[876],"SQL Performance Explained"," — index mechanics.",[27,904,905,910],{},[117,906,909],{"href":907,"rel":908},"https:\u002F\u002Fpgexercises.com",[876],"pgexercises.com"," — interactive practice.",[27,912,913,918],{},[117,914,917],{"href":915,"rel":916},"https:\u002F\u002Fmode.com\u002Fsql\u002Ftutorial",[876],"Mode SQL Tutorial"," — guided examples.",[19,920,922],{"id":921},"tooling-to-install","Tooling to Install",[924,925,927],"code-wrapper",{"language":926},"bash"